              <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-gray-600">Detection rules, threat intel matches and the alerts your connected products raise all land in one queue. A detection about an entity that already has an open case joins it: the case&rsquo;s entities and ATT&amp;CK mapping grow, and its priority rises to the detection&rsquo;s, never down. Analysts assign the case, move it from New to Investigating to Contained, read each entity&rsquo;s last seven days of activity, and close it with a verdict &mdash; True Positive, Benign Positive, False Positive or Undetermined. OneUptime AI triages each new case as it opens: it reads the detections, events, threat intel and the hosts behind them, says whether the case looks Likely Malicious, Likely Benign, Likely False Positive or Inconclusive, and suggests a priority and a playbook, every claim cited to the query behind it. It changes nothing on the case &mdash; a person sets the verdict. When a case needs the full treatment, Declare Incident opens a linked OneUptime incident, and on-call, status pages and the postmortem take over from there.</p>
